cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BoxOffice Brain: a grounded cinema-analytics agent on ClickHouse"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sarkar"
    given-names: "Dipankar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doom2quake/boxoffice"
abstract: >-
  A cinema-catalogue analytics agent on Gemini and ADK that answers plain English
  questions by writing read-only ClickHouse SQL and running it through the official
  ClickHouse MCP server at request time. Every result carries a grounding trace
  (the exact SQL, rows and bytes scanned, latency), every claim traces to a
  retrieved row, a failed query is reported as a failure rather than as an empty
  result, and a data-scope allowlist bounds what the generated SQL can read.
keywords:
  - clickhouse
  - agentic-analytics
  - grounding
  - retrieval-grounded
  - gemini-adk
  - mcp
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
